# Clerk Authentication & Authorization

This project uses **Clerk** for all authentication and authorization.

## Critical Security Principle

**Users MUST only access their own data.** Every database query that retrieves user-specific data must be filtered by the authenticated user's ID.

## Getting the User ID

### Server Components & API Routes

```typescript
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';

// Get the authenticated user's ID
const { userId } = await auth();

// Always check if user is authenticated
if (!userId) {
  return new Response('Unauthorized', { status: 401 });
}
```

### Client Components

```typescript
import { useUser } from '@clerk/nextjs';

const { user } = useUser();

// user.id contains the Clerk user ID
```

## Data Access Patterns

### ✅ CORRECT - Always filter by userId

```typescript
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';
import { db } from '@/src/db';
import { decksTable } from '@/src/db/schema';
import { eq } from 'drizzle-orm';

// Get user's decks
const { userId } = await auth();
if (!userId) throw new Error('Unauthorized');

const userDecks = await db
  .select()
  .from(decksTable)
  .where(eq(decksTable.userId, userId));
```

### ✅ CORRECT - Verify ownership before updates/deletes

```typescript
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';
import { db } from '@/src/db';
import { decksTable } from '@/src/db/schema';
import { eq, and } from 'drizzle-orm';

const { userId } = await auth();
if (!userId) throw new Error('Unauthorized');

// Update only if user owns the deck
await db
  .update(decksTable)
  .set({ name: 'Updated Name' })
  .where(and(
    eq(decksTable.id, deckId),
    eq(decksTable.userId, userId)
  ));
```

### ✅ CORRECT - Check ownership for nested resources

```typescript
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';
import { db } from '@/src/db';
import { decksTable, cardsTable } from '@/src/db/schema';
import { eq } from 'drizzle-orm';

const { userId } = await auth();
if (!userId) throw new Error('Unauthorized');

// First verify the deck belongs to the user
const [deck] = await db
  .select()
  .from(decksTable)
  .where(eq(decksTable.id, deckId));

if (!deck || deck.userId !== userId) {
  throw new Error('Unauthorized');
}

// Then get cards from that deck
const cards = await db
  .select()
  .from(cardsTable)
  .where(eq(cardsTable.deckId, deckId));
```

### ❌ WRONG - Never query without userId filter

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: This returns ALL decks for ALL users
const allDecks = await db
  .select()
  .from(decksTable);

// ❌ BAD: This allows any user to access any deck
const deck = await db
  .select()
  .from(decksTable)
  .where(eq(decksTable.id, deckId));
```

### ❌ WRONG - Never trust client-provided userId

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Client could send any userId
async function getDecks(clientUserId: string) {
  return await db
    .select()
    .from(decksTable)
    .where(eq(decksTable.userId, clientUserId));
}
```

